# This file contains examples only. Copy it to .env.test and restrict it with chmod 600 .env.test;
# .env.test is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Only e2e/setup.ts reads .env.test, at the start of `pnpm test:e2e`. A variable already set in the
# environment wins over the file. Every value here carries the TEST_ prefix, so no tool reads it by
# accident: the suite passes each TEST_X to the packed CLI as X, and gives the CLI nothing else of
# this computer's environment but PATH. Every TEST_ value is redacted from the suite's output.
#
# The offline specs (`pnpm test:e2e cli`, `pnpm test:e2e automation-progress`) need none of these.
# The machine specs (`pnpm test:e2e sprite`, `pnpm test:e2e fly-machine`) create real, paid
# workstations named oa-e2e-<run id>-...; each fails, with the CLI's own preflight message, when its
# provider token is unset. Whenever any provider token is set, every run first deletes the oa-e2e-*
# workstations an earlier, interrupted run left on that account, so set a token only for an account
# whose oa-e2e-* workstations are all the suite's.

# Fly Sprites organization token: the Sprite provider's credential, passed to the CLI as SPRITES_TOKEN.
# Required by e2e/sprite.spec.e2e.ts; also lets the start and end sweeps reach the Sprites account.
# Get one at https://sprites.dev/account. A Fly API token (FlyV1 ...) is refused.
TEST_SPRITES_TOKEN=

# Fly organization token (FlyV1 ..., fm2_... or fo1_...): the Fly Machine provider's credential,
# passed to the CLI as FLY_API_TOKEN. Required by e2e/fly-machine.spec.e2e.ts, which also needs flyctl
# (`fly`) on PATH; lets the sweeps reach the organization's Fly apps.
TEST_FLY_API_TOKEN=

# Tailscale management API key, passed to the CLI as TAILSCALE_API_KEY. Required whenever a provider
# token is set: the CLI enrols workstation devices with it, and the suite lists and deletes their
# tailnet devices with it to prove each workstation gone.
TEST_TAILSCALE_API_KEY=

# Tailnet ID, full DNS domain (yak-bebop.ts.net) or bare DNS subdomain (yak-bebop), passed to the CLI
# as TAILSCALE_TAILNET. Required whenever a provider token is set, with TEST_TAILSCALE_API_KEY.
TEST_TAILSCALE_TAILNET=

# Existing CLIProxyAPI hub URL (https://proxy.example.com or its /v1 base), passed to the CLI as
# CLIPROXYAPI_BASE_URL. Required by the machine specs' proxy create and real harness turns; a hub
# private to the tailnet is reached through it.
TEST_CLIPROXYAPI_BASE_URL=

# The hub's client credential for Claude and Codex, passed to the CLI as CLIPROXYAPI_API_KEY.
# Required together with TEST_CLIPROXYAPI_BASE_URL.
TEST_CLIPROXYAPI_API_KEY=

# Optional approved exit-node hostname, device ID or Tailscale IP, passed to the CLI as
# TAILSCALE_EXIT_NODE. Leave empty unless the tailnet's workstations must route through one.
TEST_TAILSCALE_EXIT_NODE=

# Leave both empty: the machine specs prove a create without GitHub access, which refuses to run
# while a GitHub token reaches the CLI. Any other TEST_X set here reaches the CLI as X too.
TEST_GH_TOKEN=
TEST_GITHUB_TOKEN=
